---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TrustBar from '../../../components/TrustBar.astro';
import Price from '../../../components/Price.astro';
import CTASection from '../../../components/CTASection.astro';
import { site } from '../../../config';

const wa = `https://wa.me/${site.whatsapp}?text=${encodeURIComponent('Hi CQ Buddy! I want local support for my trip (¥200/order). My dates are around: ')}`;
---
<Base title="Local Concierge — Remote Support ¥200/order | CQ Buddy" description="A real Chongqing local on WhatsApp for your first 72 hours: payments, apps, transport, translation, restaurant calls and re-planning. ¥200 per order, up to 4 travellers, 30-minute first response.">
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Remote · 72-hour trip window · 1–4 travellers</p>
      <h1>Your local contact for the first 72 hours.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.2rem;max-width:46ch;">Not a bot, not a call centre — one named local on your WhatsApp, from the day before you fly until you're settled in Chongqing. Ask anything, in plain English.</p>
      <p><Price cny={200} unit="per order · up to 4 travellers" id="price" /></p>
      <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/en/booking/?product=concierge">Request local support</a>
        &nbsp;
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={wa} rel="noopener">Try us on WhatsApp first</a>
      </p>
      <p class="muted small">{site.responsePromise}, {site.supportHours}. ¥100 deposit after we confirm scope and capacity — never before.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="white" style="padding-top:1rem;">
    <div class="container"><TrustBar /></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What's included</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>72 hours of WhatsApp support for your whole travel party (one group chat)</li>
            <li>A free 20-minute planning call before you fly — apps, eSIM, realistic expectations</li>
            <li>Payment and ride-hailing app setup, walked through screen by screen</li>
            <li>On-the-spot translation: menus, signs, pharmacy labels, driver questions</li>
            <li>Restaurant bookings and re-planning when weather or delays wreck your day</li>
            <li>Up to 2 short calls to restaurants, hotels or drivers per order (≤15 min each)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What's not included</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>No airport pickup or in-person guiding — this is a remote service</li>
            <li>No paying on your behalf, no continuous interpretation, no ticket purchasing service</li>
            <li>No medical or legal advice — we help you communicate with professionals</li>
            <li>Not a 24/7 hotline: real replies within 30 minutes, {site.supportHours}</li>
            <li>We can't guarantee a foreign bank card passes every app's checks — we maximise the odds and have fallbacks ready</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="white">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">How the window runs</p>
      <h2>Before you fly, while you land, after you're settled.</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><h3>Free planning call</h3><p>20 minutes, any time before departure: which apps to install, eSIM choice, your first-day plan, honest answers about money and connectivity.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><h3>Window starts when you say</h3><p>The day before you fly, landing day, or mid-trip — you pick. 72 hours from that moment, Beijing time, confirmed in writing.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><h3>Ask anything</h3><p>Photograph the menu, share the error screen, ask "is this price fair?" One chat, up to four travellers, one local who answers personally.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><h3>Backup when we rest</h3><p>Overlapping windows are capped at three so nobody is over-committed. If your contact is briefly unavailable, a named backup covers.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">The planning call is free and doesn't start your paid window.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Typical moments (examples)</p>
      <h2>What people actually ask.</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card"><h3>"My card was declined"</h3><p>Screenshot the error — we identify which step failed, which fallback works, and what to tell your bank.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>"The hotel can't read my name"</h3><p>We join by phone, spell it in Chinese, confirm the registration went through.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>"Is this taxi legit?"</h3><p>Photograph the plate and the meter — straight answers from someone who knows the local tells.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>"Rain killed my gorge trip"</h3><p>We rebuild the day around indoor options and rebook the table you'd pinned.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>"What's in this dish?"</h3><p>Menu photo in, ingredient list and spice level out — plus the phrase to order the mild version.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>"The pharmacy label"</h3><p>Send a photo; we translate dosage instructions and confirm with the pharmacist by phone if needed.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">Examples of the kind of help we give — your window is yours to spend.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="white">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Refunds, in one breath</p>
      <h2>Cancel before your window starts: full refund.<br />Unhappy in the first 30 minutes of real service: full refund.</h2>
      <p>The full text is two minutes' reading: <a href="/en/legal/refunds/">refund policy →</a>. No-shopping rules apply to everything we touch, remote or not: <a href="/en/legal/no-shopping/">the promise →</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Good to know</p>
      <h2>Questions we hear a lot.</h2>
      <details><summary>When exactly do the 72 hours start and end?</summary><p>Whenever you choose — the day before departure, landing day, or mid-trip. Start and end are fixed in writing (Beijing time) when you book, so there's no ambiguity at the airport.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is this a 24/7 hotline?</summary><p>No — and we'll never pretend otherwise. Real people reply within 30 minutes during {site.supportHours}. Outside those hours your message waits and gets answered as soon as we're back. True emergencies in China: 110 / 119 / 120 first, then message us to help you communicate.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you come to the airport or my hotel?</summary><p>No. This service is deliberately remote — that's what keeps it ¥200 instead of ¥2,000. In-person welcomes are our First Night product (currently inquiry-only while we build the team).</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you pay for things on my behalf?</summary><p>No. We guide you through paying yourself; your money never passes through us, and we take zero commission on anything you buy.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if I don't use WhatsApp?</summary><p>Tell us — email or another channel you already use works. We agree one backup channel before your window starts, so a single blocked app never strands you.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you guarantee my bank card will link to payment apps?</summary><p>Honestly, no — the final check is always the app's own risk engine. What we guarantee: correct setup sequence, the known-good card path, and a working fallback (cash guidance + offline options) if a card refuses.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can the four of us all message you?</summary><p>One group chat, whole travel party, one concierge. One phone or four — same price, same service.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection primary sku="Local Concierge" heading="One local on WhatsApp. That's the whole pitch." />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Service', name: 'Local Concierge (Remote)',
    serviceType: 'Remote travel assistance', areaServed: 'Chongqing, China',
    provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'CQ Buddy' },
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '200', priceCurrency: 'CNY' },
  })} />
</Base>
